# Waterbender Ascension, "Waterbend {4}: Target creature can't be blocked this turn" (CR 701.67a-b, 509.1b, 611.2). Bot1 casts the enchantment and a
# Grizzly Bears on turn 1 with four Moxen. On turn 3 it pays {4} with one Mox's mana and three taps of its other Moxen: nothing is left in the pool and
# the Bears, which could also have been tapped, are untapped. The target is a Mox, which is no creature and is refused, or Bot1's own Bears, accepted
# (any creature will do, not just an opponent's). Bot2's Bears may not block them, and the Bears' damage puts the first
# quest counter on the enchantment. On turn 5 the effect has worn off: Bot2's Bears block.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Mox Emerald
Mox Ruby
Waterbender Ascension
Grizzly Bears
Island
Island x20

[Bot2 Deck]
